        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Heat Pumps",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "A heat pump is a refrigeration system with a reversing valve. In cooling mode it's an\nair conditioner. In heating mode it runs the refrigerant cycle backwards — extracting\nheat from outdoor air and delivering it indoors. The critical insight: you're not\ncreating heat, you're moving it. Moving heat requires less work than creating it."
    },
    {
      "id": "05-HEAT-PUMPS.md#003",
      "path": [
        "05-HEAT-PUMPS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:hvac:05-heat-pumps, git-history:hvac:05-heat-pumps]",
        "canonical_path": "hvac/05-HEAT-PUMPS.md",
        "concepts": "[heat, pumps]",
        "current_path": "hvac/05-HEAT-PUMPS.md",
        "id": "maxim:hvac:heat-pumps",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "hvac",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[heat, pumps]",
        "section": "hvac",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Heat Pumps",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+----------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                    HEAT PUMP OPERATING MODES                         |\n|                                                                      |\n|  COOLING MODE (Summer)          HEATING MODE (Winter)                |\n|  -----------------------        -----------------------              |\n|  Indoor coil = EVAPORATOR       Indoor coil = CONDENSER              |\n|  Absorbs heat from room         Releases heat to room                |\n|  Cools + dehumidifies           Warms the space                      |\n|                                                                      |\n|  Outdoor coil = CONDENSER       Outdoor coil = EVAPORATOR            |\n|  Rejects heat to outside        Absorbs heat from outdoor air        |\n|                                                                      |\n|                    REVERSING VALVE switches direction                |\n|                    (four-way valve in refrigerant circuit)           |\n|                                                                      |\n|  COP (cooling): 3–5             COP (heating): 2–4 at 47°F           |\n|  = more efficient than AC       = more efficient than gas furnace    |\n|    vs. gas furnace (COP < 1)    in most conditions                   |\n+----------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
