      "text": "## Section 1: The Physics — Why COP > 1"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-HEAT-PUMPS.md#006",
      "path": [
        "05-HEAT-PUMPS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:hvac:05-heat-pumps, git-history:hvac:05-heat-pumps]",
        "canonical_path": "hvac/05-HEAT-PUMPS.md",
        "concepts": "[heat, pumps]",
        "current_path": "hvac/05-HEAT-PUMPS.md",
        "id": "maxim:hvac:heat-pumps",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "hvac",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[heat, pumps]",
        "section": "hvac",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Heat Pumps",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The Carnot bound for heat pump heating: COP_max = T_hot / (T_hot - T_cold) in Kelvin. Heating to 70F (294K) when outdoor is 20F (266K): COP_max = 294 / 28 = 10.5. Real ASHP at those conditions: COP 2-3, or 20-30% of Carnot. The key relationship: COP_max is proportional to 1/delta-T — as outdoor temperature drops, delta-T increases and COP_max falls steeply. This is why the performance-vs-temperature curve below has its characteristic shape, and why supplemental heat (electric resistance or gas) kicks in at extreme cold."
    },
    {
      "id": "05-HEAT-PUMPS.md#007",
      "path": [
        "05-HEAT-PUMPS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:hvac:05-heat-pumps, git-history:hvac:05-heat-pumps]",
        "canonical_path": "hvac/05-HEAT-PUMPS.md",
        "concepts": "[heat, pumps]",
        "current_path": "hvac/05-HEAT-PUMPS.md",
        "id": "maxim:hvac:heat-pumps",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "hvac",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[heat, pumps]",
        "section": "hvac",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Heat Pumps",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  GAS FURNACE:                  HEAT PUMP:\n  ┌──────────────────┐          ┌──────────────────────────────────┐\n  │ Chemical energy  │          │ Electrical energy (work) in:     │\n  │ (gas) burned     │          │ W = 1 BTU                        │\n  │ → heat directly  │          └──────────────────────────────────┘\n  │ AFUE 80–98%      │                      |\n  │ COP ≤ 0.98       │                      v Compressor work\n  └──────────────────┘          ┌──────────────────────────────────┐\n                                │ Outdoor air at 20°F contains     │\n  ENERGY IN = ENERGY OUT        │ heat (absolute zero = -459°F;    │\n  (some lost up flue)           │ 20°F = 479°F above absolute zero)│\n                                │ → Heat absorbed from outdoor air │\n                                │   by evaporating refrigerant     │\n                                └──────────────────────────────────┘\n                                              |\n                                              v\n                                ┌──────────────────────────────────┐\n                                │ Heat delivered indoors:          │\n                                │ Q = W + Q_outdoor                │\n                                │   = 1 + 2 = 3 BTU                │\n                                │ COP = Q/W = 3.0                  │\n                                │ (300% \"efficiency\")              │\n                                └──────────────────────────────────┘"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-HEAT-PUMPS.md#008",
      "path": [
        "05-HEAT-PUMPS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:hvac:05-heat-pumps, git-history:hvac:05-heat-pumps]",
        "canonical_path": "hvac/05-HEAT-PUMPS.md",
        "concepts": "[heat, pumps]",
        "current_path": "hvac/05-HEAT-PUMPS.md",
        "id": "maxim:hvac:heat-pumps",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "hvac",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[heat, pumps]",
        "section": "hvac",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Heat Pumps",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Not magic — work moves ambient heat uphill against ΔT\n  Second law: work required is proportional to temperature lift\n  Smaller temperature difference (mild outdoor) → higher COP\n  Larger temperature difference (very cold outdoor) → lower COP\n```"
    },
