      "text": "## Section 2: Air-Source Heat Pump (ASHP) — Standard"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-HEAT-PUMPS.md#011",
      "path": [
        "05-HEAT-PUMPS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:hvac:05-heat-pumps, git-history:hvac:05-heat-pumps]",
        "canonical_path": "hvac/05-HEAT-PUMPS.md",
        "concepts": "[heat, pumps]",
        "current_path": "hvac/05-HEAT-PUMPS.md",
        "id": "maxim:hvac:heat-pumps",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "hvac",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[heat, pumps]",
        "section": "hvac",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Heat Pumps",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  BASIC ASHP:\n  - Same components as AC + reversing valve\n  - Outdoor unit handles both condensing (cooling) and evaporating (heating)\n  - Balance point: outdoor temp where heat pump output = building heat loss\n  - Below balance point: auxiliary electric resistance strips supplement"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-HEAT-PUMPS.md#012",
      "path": [
        "05-HEAT-PUMPS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:hvac:05-heat-pumps, git-history:hvac:05-heat-pumps]",
        "canonical_path": "hvac/05-HEAT-PUMPS.md",
        "concepts": "[heat, pumps]",
        "current_path": "hvac/05-HEAT-PUMPS.md",
        "id": "maxim:hvac:heat-pumps",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "hvac",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[heat, pumps]",
        "section": "hvac",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Heat Pumps",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "TRADITIONAL BALANCE POINT: ~25–30°F\n  Below 25°F: COP drops, aux strips kick in (COP = 1.0)\n  → Operating cost penalty; efficiency advantage disappears in deep cold\n  → Traditional ASHP problematic in climate zones 5+"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-HEAT-PUMPS.md#013",
      "path": [
        "05-HEAT-PUMPS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
