      "text": "## Section 3: Cold-Climate ASHP"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-HEAT-PUMPS.md#021",
      "path": [
        "05-HEAT-PUMPS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:hvac:05-heat-pumps, git-history:hvac:05-heat-pumps]",
        "canonical_path": "hvac/05-HEAT-PUMPS.md",
        "concepts": "[heat, pumps]",
        "current_path": "hvac/05-HEAT-PUMPS.md",
        "id": "maxim:hvac:heat-pumps",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "hvac",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[heat, pumps]",
        "section": "hvac",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Heat Pumps",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The engineering problem: as outdoor temp drops, air density decreases, evaporator\ncoil performance degrades, and more compression work is required. Standard ASHPs\nhit their performance floor at ~25°F."
    },
    {
      "id": "05-HEAT-PUMPS.md#022",
      "path": [
        "05-HEAT-PUMPS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:hvac:05-heat-pumps, git-history:hvac:05-heat-pumps]",
        "canonical_path": "hvac/05-HEAT-PUMPS.md",
        "concepts": "[heat, pumps]",
        "current_path": "hvac/05-HEAT-PUMPS.md",
        "id": "maxim:hvac:heat-pumps",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "hvac",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[heat, pumps]",
        "section": "hvac",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Heat Pumps",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  COLD-CLIMATE ASHP TECHNOLOGIES:\n  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │ Variable-speed/inverter compressor                              │\n  │ → Runs at higher speed in cold (compensates for less heat       │\n  │   in air) → maintains capacity at low temperatures              │\n  │                                                                 │\n  │ Enhanced Vapor Injection (EVI) / Intermediate Injection         │\n  │ → Injects additional refrigerant vapor mid-compression          │\n  │ → Increases refrigerant mass flow → more capacity in cold       │\n  │ → Reduces discharge temperature → protects compressor           │\n  │                                                                 │\n  │ Flash tank / Economizer cycle                                   │\n  │ → Intermediate pressure stage for additional heat exchange      │\n  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-HEAT-PUMPS.md#023",
      "path": [
        "05-HEAT-PUMPS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
